lesson:
An ARRAY holds many values of one type:  int runes[3] = {5, 8, 2};
  Indexes start at ZERO:  runes[0] == 5,  runes[2] == 2.
  std::vector is a magical array that can GROW:  (#include <vector>)
    std::vector<int> v = {1, 2};   v.push_back(3);   v.size() == 3
  Range-for loops visit each element:  for (int r : v) { ... }

lessonCode:
std::vector<std::string> spells = {"Fire", "Ice"};
spells.push_back("Lightning");
for (const auto& s : spells) {
    std::cout << s << "\n";
}
std::cout << spells.size(); // 3

